        "name": "USN-5331-2",
        "description": "USN-5331-1 fixed several vulnerabilities in tcpdump. This update provides the corresponding update for Ubuntu 18.04 LTS and Ubuntu 20.04 LTS.   Original advisory details:  It was discovered that tcpdump incorrectly handled certain inputs.  An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service,  or possibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2018-16301)    It was discovered that tcpdump incorrectly handled certain captured data.  An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service.  (CVE-2020-8037)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2018-16301",
          "CVE-2020-8037"
        ]
      },
